## SQ-VP-04 | /vtdtest tags
# setup (this row): the s1home marker at the world spawn and the rhome marker at 1000 -60 1000 (its chunk is
# forceloaded BEFORE the summon: r1103 p2 summoned into an unloaded chunk and every R row lost its capture)
bootexpect Done \(
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s1home] run summon minecraft:marker ~ ~ ~ {Tags:["s1home"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s1home,limit=1] Pos
capture H entity data: \[(-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d\]
> forceload add {H1-32} {H3-56} {H1+96} {H3+48}
> forceload add 192 16 304 48
> forceload add 1000 1000
sleep 3
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=rhome] run summon minecraft:marker 1000 -60 1000 {Tags:["rhome"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=rhome,limit=1] Pos
capture R entity data: \[(-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d\]
> forceload add {R1-16} {R3-16} {R1+80} {R3+150}
> forceload add 96 496 340 560
sleep 5
> gamerule doDaylightCycle false
> weather clear 100000
> difficulty easy
> vtdtest tags
waitlog \[vtdtest\] done tags 120
expect \[vtdtest\] done tags: \d+ pass, 0 fail
reject \[vtdtest\] FAIL

## SQ-CDF-06 | cake pan half: the oven's cake recipes name the pan in their tool field (not an ingredient)
# r1103 p2: `zq uses` reads getIngredients only, and BakingRecipe keeps the bakeware in getTool(), so "0 uses" was the
# probe's blind spot. rdetail+ prints the tool field. Mortar, seasoning and the milk jar halves passed in r1103 p2.
> zq bytype creativeengineering:baking
> zq rdetail baking/carrot_cake
> zq rdetail cake
expect bytype creativeengineering:baking: [1-9]\d*
expect rdetail\+ \S*baking/\S* fields: tool .*cake_pan
look the cake-pan tool lines name oven cake recipes (carrot cake and the pack cakes)

